  "blurb": "A four-bedroom, five-bathroom hillside villa in Chaweng Noi, facing due east across Chaweng Bay so every bedroom wakes to the sunrise. Walls of glass open onto an infinity pool on the edge of the view. Sold fully furnished and ready to move into — 534 m² built on an 817 m² plot, five minutes from the beach.",
  "detail": "High in the hills above Chaweng Noi, this villa is set on the slope so that nothing stands between it and the Gulf. The outlook runs east over Chaweng Bay, which means mornings arrive over the water — and each of the four bedrooms has been placed to catch them.\n\nThe architecture is spare and white, stepped down the hillside in clean horizontal levels. Floor-to-ceiling glass wraps the open-plan living and dining space, and a Western-style kitchen sits alongside, so cooking, eating and lounging all share the same wide view. Beyond the glass, an infinity pool with sun loungers runs along the terrace edge, with further sitting areas tucked into the natural granite of the site.\n\nAll four bedrooms are en-suite, and the house has five bathrooms in total, some with freestanding tubs set against the sea. The interiors are finished in a calm, minimal palette with bright accents of original art, and the villa is offered fully furnished — ready for immediate use as a private home or to continue as a holiday rental.\n\nThe plot is 817 m² with 534 m² of built area, with private parking and an easy approach road. The beach is around five minutes away, Central Festival's restaurants and shops are close by, and Samui International Airport is roughly twenty minutes' drive.",
